# qwen3-30b-a3b-jetson — Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 for the mt100 board
#
# Build:   ollama create qwen3-30b-a3b-jetson -f infra/ollama/Modelfile.qwen3-30b-a3b-jetson
# Profile: apps/llm/model_profiles.py ("local_ollama/qwen3-30b-a3b-jetson")
#
# The 30B arm of the mt100 size ladder. A3B = ~3B active parameters per token,
# so decode cost tracks a 3B model while capacity tracks 30B. Laptop/Colab
# class, NOT the 8 GB Jetson — read its numbers as a capacity ceiling, not a
# deployment candidate.
#
# INSTRUCT MODE comes from the BASE MODEL, not a runtime flag. The bare
# qwen3:30b-a3b tag is the hybrid checkpoint; instruct-2507 has no thinking to
# suppress, so the profile deliberately sets no ollama_think. This is the same
# rule Modelfile.qwen3-4b-jetson states: enforce instruct with the checkpoint
# where one exists, because ollama_think=False only disables Ollama's parser on
# templates that open <think> unconditionally.
#
# NOTE the FULL quantisation suffix. ollama publishes instruct-2507 only as
# -q4_K_M (18.6 GB), -q8_0 (32.5 GB) and -fp16 (61.1 GB); there is no
# unquantised alias and no bare `-q4`. q4_K_M matches the quantisation the
# other tags on this board use.
#
# The suffix is load-bearing and easy to truncate: `qwen3:30b-a3b-instruct-2507-q4`
# (without _K_M) 404s at pull time — "pull model manifest: file does not exist" —
# and run_matrix.sh then skips the arm, so a Colab session builds nothing. That
# happened on 2026-08-10, from a tags-page scrape whose character class omitted
# the underscore. Verify any change here against
# https://registry.ollama.ai/v2/library/qwen3/manifests/<tag> returning 200;
# test_modelfile_from_tags_resolve_on_the_registry covers the current set.
FROM qwen3:30b-a3b-instruct-2507-q4_K_M

# Must match local_ollama/qwen3-30b-a3b-jetson in apps/llm/model_profiles.py.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
